'm rejecting PKT-0042. The work is good, but one surprise from the executor's log isn't kept in any test or baseline, and that is a mandatory rejection for a characterize packet.\n\n**What holds up**\n- **Goal:** all four directions the server uses are covered: open → Editor.bin, save from Editor.bin back to docx/xlsx/pptx, pdf, and odf. A fifth direction, own (docx/xlsx/pptx to the same format), is extra.\n- **Contract and budget:** 5 files and 316 lines, against limits of 6 files and 800 lines. No existing file is modified except the packet and `friction.jsonl`.\n- **Executor log:** filled in. No follow-ups were requested, and none appear in `.theseus/spawn/`.\n- **PDF checks:** PDFs are compared by page count and a hash of the normalized text, never by bytes. That is the right call.\n- **`diff` logic:** a missing direction or a missing file is flagged, an output appearing or disappearing is flagged, and the size tolerance is relative to the baseline.\n- **Surprises 1 and 3 are kept:** the baseline records the empty templates' PDFs with `textChars: 0`, and the committed baseline pins the run-to-run determinism.\n\n**Blocking: surprise 2 is not kept anywhere**\n- The log says a wrong `m_nFormatTo` makes x2t return exit 88 with no output. The executor calls this \"worth knowing for the exit-code invariant\".\n- Nothing in `corpus.py` or `baseline-9.3.7-1.json` records it. The baseline has only exit 0, so a later x2t build that changed this exit code would pass the oracle unnoticed.\n- The fix is small: run one conversion per sample (or one fixed sample) with a format code x2t doesn't support (e.g. 258), and record `exit: 88` and `size: 0` in the baseline so `diff` checks it.\n\n**Non-blocking, worth fixing in the same pass**\n- **Corpus folder name:** results are keyed by the corpus folder's name, so the baseline only matches if `make-corpus.py` writes to a folder named `corpus`. The usage line in the Atlas lessons says `<make-corpus out>` without saying this. Anyone who picks another name gets \"only in baseline/new\" differences instead of a real comparison. Either state the required name or key results by file name only.\n- **Generation dates:** `make-corpus.py` fixes the random seed, but python-docx, openpyxl and python-pptx write the current date into the documents. Regenerated inputs therefore differ in bytes from run to run. The text hash isn't affected, but the log should say \"deterministic content\" rather than \"deterministic\".\n\nVERDICT: REJECT surprise \"wrong m_nFormatTo gives exit 88 with no output\" is in the log but not kept in a test/baseline; add an unsupported-format case to corpus.py and baseline-9.3.7-1.json (and document that the make-corpus output dir must be named `corpus`)","ttft_ms":2150,"type":"result","duration_ms":23328,"uuid":"2f13a91e-4274-4a65-a49a-c4d6b589678a","ttft_stream_ms":1003,"time_to_request_ms":434,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":301,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":24,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":12,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":7,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":13,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":9,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":23,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":5,"request_build":10},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":43,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":163,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":214,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":139,"process_rss_mib_result":227,"process_anon_mib_result":138,"process_peak_rss_mib":252,"process_cpu_ms_turn":1057,"process_wall_ms_turn":23327,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":514,"process_wall_ms_streaming":20217,"main_stream_count":5,"main_stream_event_count":308,"main_stream_chunk_count":119,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_produce